{"ts": 0.210177, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 4 · Commands, streams, composition\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93mtask\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 227}
{"ts": 0.210216, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.212252, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mSTAGE 4 — GATE TASK\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nWork inside \u001b[94m/var/folders/jx/f_4n055973x5cwnyh_mhlw9h0000gn/T/shelltutor-sim-home-0x4axnbn/stage4\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\nDo these:\r\n\r\n  1. Use \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m and a pipe to count from 1 to 100 and save\r\n     the count to \u001b[94mcount.txt\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n  2. Use a glob to list every \u001b[94m*.txt\u001b[0m file in this folder.\r\n\r\nThen type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[90mI will check: count.txt exists and contains 100, and that you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90mlisted the .txt files with a glob.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mcheck\u001b[93m when done.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 529}
{"ts": 0.212696, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
{"ts": 0.230916, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[95mcheck\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ test your work\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mshow\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ the task again\u001b[0m   \u001b[95mquit\u001b[0m\u001b[90m ▸ save and leave\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 132}
{"ts": 0.230973, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.231039, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "seq 1 100 | wc -l > count.txt\n", "len": 30}
{"ts": 0.23109, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "seq 1 100 | wc -l > count.txt\r\n", "len": 31}
{"ts": 0.231105, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 9}
